            "32x32" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "48x48" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png"
         },
         "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
         "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
         "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
      },
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i0044v:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "The format strings (timezone related) %z %Z appear only supported in std c++ for ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/manip/put_time"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/manip/put_time",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "not get_time.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But they both make similar sense. And the support in the current stdc++ lib is unfortunate (for Stroika) because it refers to the global system time (or maybe based on TZ)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Instead, the right thing for the DateTime class - with its PARSE and FORMAT methods, would be to use its associated timezone.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "For BOTH Parse() and Format() - this can be done relatively easily by ourselves parsing the format string (%A %B etc) - and for nearly all of them, just calling the time_put/time_get variant to handle the string, but for the %z %Z strings - we handle directly.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
